Portions of twowindow_sim.py are taken from twosfs
(https://github.com/desai-lab/twosfs, commit 069d84d6), the package of
Daniel P. Rice, Eliot F. Fenton, John Novembre and Michael M. Desai that
accompanies Fenton, Rice, Novembre and Desai, Genetics 229 (2025) iyaf023,
released under the MIT License:

  seed_from_name      is filename2seed of twosfs/simulations.py;
  root_seed and the per-batch seed draws
                      follow the seed scheme of twosfs (run name -> hash ->
                      numpy Generator -> msprime seeds);
  _run_2w, _accumulate
                      the tskit call allele_frequency_spectrum(mode="branch",
                      windows=..., polarised=True, span_normalise=False) is
                      written as in twosfs/spectra.py.

